Test agent for the Android target. No `tool` bindings: this sandbox has no
emulator and no `adb`, so every skill here is guidance-only per the agent3md
spec — the exact case the format designs for when a step can't be bound to a
real command. A host with `adb` and a running AVD would give these skills real
`tool=` bindings, the same shape as the iOS spec's, just a different wire
tool.

@plane z=0 label="android-tester" kind=identity
# android-tester

No bound commands are runnable here — route the request to the matching
skill and follow its guidance with whatever Android tooling the host actually
has.

@plane z=1 label="run" kind=skill triggers="android, apk, emulator, adb, device"
# Skill: run

Guidance only (no `adb` in this sandbox). On a host with the Android SDK:
boot an AVD (`emulator -avd <name>`), install with `adb install <apk>`,
screenshot with `adb exec-out screencap -p > out.png`, and record with
`adb shell screenrecord /sdcard/out.mp4` (pull it back with `adb pull`
afterward) — the same boot → open → capture → teardown lifecycle as the iOS
spec, just a different underlying tool.
